# Presentation stage

Inputs:

- `instructions` — the `## Data presentation` markdown (untrusted).
- `appendix_scripts` — current Appendix presentation scripts.
- `run_order` — the Appendix's declared run order.
- `data_dir` — read inference outputs from this dir.

## Task

For each presentation instruction:

1. If the existing Appendix script still matches the instruction,
   keep it.
2. Otherwise, generate or patch a self-contained uv script (PEP 723
   metadata pinned to python 3.12 / pandas>=2.2,<2.3 /
   numpy>=1.26,<2.3) that reads inference outputs under `data_dir`
   and emits the Result-subsection body to stdout.
3. Derive each script's `result_heading` from its instruction (the
   name of the subsection the stdout feeds, e.g.
   `Milestone-PreProdIssues`). Unless the instruction asks for a
   file under `data_dir`, the stdout IS the Result subsection body.
4. Run it:

   ```bash
   cd {{ input.data_dir }}
   uv run -p 3.12 <name>.py <argv...>
   ```

   Fix issues as they surface and re-run.

## Output

```bash
$LOOM output init {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }}
$LOOM output add  {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }} \
    --set-json 'scripts=[]' --set-json 'run_order=[]' \
    --set-json 'runs=[]'
# per script:
$LOOM output add  {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }} \
    --set 'scripts[].name=<name>' \
    --set 'scripts[-1].description=<one-liner>' \
    --set 'scripts[-1].source=<full source>' \
    --set-json 'scripts[-1].run_argv=["<arg1>"]' \
    --set 'run_order[]=<name>'
# per run (include result_heading):
$LOOM output add  {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }} \
    --set 'runs[].name=<name>' \
    --set 'runs[-1].exit_code=<int>' \
    --set 'runs[-1].stdout=<...>' \
    --set 'runs[-1].stderr=<...>' \
    --set 'runs[-1].duration_s=<float>' \
    --set-json 'runs[-1].output_paths=[]' \
    --set 'runs[-1].result_heading=<result subsection heading>'
```
